# Cypher Core — local configuration template.
# Copy to .env for local development. In Vercel, add the same names under
# Settings > Environment Variables. Never commit the real .env.

# --- Build-time values read by the browser -------------------------------------
# VITE_ names are inlined into the public bundle at build time, so add them as type
# "Config" (not "Secret") and redeploy after changing them. The anon key is public by
# design: row-level security decides what it can reach, and it can reach nothing without
# a signed-in session. Without these two, the app renders but refuses to sign in.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-PUBLIC-ANON-KEY

# Optional: only set this if the gateway service is hosted on another origin.
# VITE_API_BASE=https://your-app.vercel.app/api

# --- Server-side only (api/index.py) -------------------------------------------
# Same project, same public anon key — but these must NOT carry a VITE_ prefix, because
# the gateway is the component that decides whether a caller is validated and inside the
# rate limit. Add them in Vercel as type "Secret".
#
#   SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-PUBLIC-ANON-KEY
#
# If either is missing the gateway answers 503 and sign-in is refused. There is no
# fallback path that skips validation.
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-PUBLIC-ANON-KEY

# The service_role key is not used anywhere in this project and must never be added:
# it bypasses row-level security, which is the only thing separating one vault from
# another.
